Z||000000||bHooper||05-17-2000||09:53 PM||||i am missing a few heat shields... one in particular is the one for the slave cylinder (v-6).  although, at this point, i dont think that i can reattach the ones for the crossover.<P>has anyone ever fabricated their own heat shields?  i was thinking of trying to use the flexible exhaust pipe, somehow.<P>any thoughts?<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||05-17-2000||10:03 PM||||Aluminum roofing flashing. Thin, easy to work, stays where it's put unless something hits it. Remember heat sheilds don't insulate like fiberglass. They reflect heat instead. You could use tin foil for them if you wanted and it would be just as effective.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||05-17-2000||10:58 PM||||My '88 v-6 5-speed has no heat shield for the slave, and I don't think it ever did. It does have the heat shield on the y-pipe, and I have never had any problems with the current setup. Just something to think about. I personally wouldn't worry about it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiasco||05-18-2000||03:26 PM||||I don't have one either, on my '85 2.8's slave, as I said in your slave cyl. post.<BR>Doesn't Fiero store have that exhaust wrap tape stuff? If you're really conerned, that might do it. Does anyone use the stuff?||||reg||1
